2
00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.514
(DANCE MUSIC PLAYING)

3
00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:45.644
ALL: (CHANTING)
Retchid Kat! Retchid Kat!

4
00:00:54.588 --> 00:00:57.319
They love you. Kill 'em.

5
00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:10.560
(CROWD CHEERING)

6
00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:11.900
SAMMY: Yeah.

7
00:01:12.506 --> 00:01:13.906
Yeah. the Kat.

8
00:01:14.875 --> 00:01:16.571
Yeah.

9
00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:21.879
(SAMMY WHOOPING)

10
00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:31.388
(TECHNO MUSIC PLAYING)

11
00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:53.604
(STRING QUARTET PLAYING)

12
00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:27.239
No. no. no. no.

13
00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:31.115
Mr. Brimley. it is
a violin. not a saw.

14
00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:33.547
We only have till
Saturday to get this right.

15
00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.112
We can stay here
all night if we have to.

16
00:02:37.658 --> 00:02:39.024
Carter. dude. get it right.

17
00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:40.788
LAWSON: Again from the 14th.

18
00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:45.825
(TECHNO MUSIC PLAYING)

19
00:03:15.696 --> 00:03:16.891
(CLATTERING)

20
00:03:39.086 --> 00:03:40.418
(CAR ENGINE STARTING)

21
00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:43.914
(CLASSICAL MUSIC
PLAYING ON RADIO)

22
00:03:48.862 --> 00:03:50.228
(RAT SQUEAKING)

23
00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:54.766
(RATS SQUEALING)

24
00:03:58.138 --> 00:04:00.369
(SCREAMING)

25
00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:10.978
(SCREAMING)

26
00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:17.389
MAN: <i>The terror</i>

27
00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:03.495
(SCREAMING)

28
00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:09.135
Ooh. smoothies.

29
00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:10.540
I need some ice.

30
00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.278
It's in the freezer.

31
00:05:15.549 --> 00:05:17.279
I'm just warming up first.

32
00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:19.319
It's going to be
cold over there.

33
00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:21.081
You should've
started this earlier.

34
00:05:22.823 --> 00:05:24.155
I think we have a problem.

35
00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:25.815
All right. We can go upstairs.

36
00:05:25.926 --> 00:05:28.293
With the ice. There isn't any.

37
00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:29.659
Oh. no.

38
00:05:33.767 --> 00:05:36.066
It's warm. Everything's
going to spoil.

39
00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:38.381
How much of this do you
think we can fit in the blender?

40
00:05:38.405 --> 00:05:39.930
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

41
00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:41.734
Yeah. Burkhardt.

42
00:05:42.776 --> 00:05:43.937
Where?

43
00:05:50.684 --> 00:05:52.084
Detectives
Burkhardt and Griffin.

44
00:05:52.152 --> 00:05:53.848
this is Assistant
Principal Grace Kaplan.

45
00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:56.389
She found the body
about an hour ago.

46
00:05:56.456 --> 00:05:59.085
Says it's Paul Lawson.
a music teacher here.

47
00:05:59.159 --> 00:06:01.219
He was the director
of the music program.

48
00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:04.992
I just can't believe this has
happened. It's so horrible.

49
00:06:05.065 --> 00:06:06.676
Well. do you want to
tell us what happened?

50
00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:08.965
I saw the car when I
came in this morning.

51
00:06:09.369 --> 00:06:11.113
It's a little unusual for
anyone to be here before me.

52
00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:12.765
that's why I walked
over to the car.

53
00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:16.771
I'm sorry. It's okay.

54
00:06:17.744 --> 00:06:19.736
Looks to me like it
happened sometime last night.

55
00:06:19.846 --> 00:06:21.086
He's been dead for a few hours.

56
00:06:21.147 --> 00:06:23.343
Car's locked. We
kept it that way.

57
00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:25.851
Got some evidence inside.
didn't want it to get away.

58
00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:28.052
Death by rat?

59
00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:29.519
WU: Looks like.

60
00:06:30.023 --> 00:06:32.015
Oh. God. rats. I
can't stand rats.

61
00:06:32.092 --> 00:06:33.151
NICK: Coroner here?

62
00:06:33.226 --> 00:06:34.990
Yeah. waiting for you.
So is Animal Control.

63
00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:37.273
Nobody wants to open the
door until you guys give the okay.

64
00:06:37.297 --> 00:06:39.095
Fingerprints done?
Yeah. we're good to go.

65
00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:40.564
Open it up.

66
00:06:40.767 --> 00:06:41.767
Let's go.

67
00:06:49.476 --> 00:06:51.001
(WOMAN SCREAMING)

68
00:06:55.048 --> 00:06:56.209
Ooh.

69
00:06:56.716 --> 00:06:59.345
We also found some cages in
the bushes you should look at.

70
00:07:03.757 --> 00:07:06.317
Whoever chucked these didn't
make much of an effort to hide them.

71
00:07:06.493 --> 00:07:09.190
Geiger Pest Control.
We know them?

72
00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:11.288
They're in northeast
Portland. by the river.

73
00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:12.932
According to the
Assistant Principal.

74
00:07:12.999 --> 00:07:14.467
Lawson was here late last night

75
00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:17.207
rehearsing for a school performance
supposed to happen on Saturday.

76
00:07:17.771 --> 00:07:19.205
Glad I'm not a ticket holder.

77
00:07:19.272 --> 00:07:21.207
Anyone see him
leave? Still checking.

78
00:07:21.508 --> 00:07:23.773
But we got names of the four
students he was rehearsing.

79
00:07:29.716 --> 00:07:31.014
HANK: Nice house.

80
00:07:32.018 --> 00:07:33.281
Nice cars.

81
00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:35.889
And bad things still happen.

82
00:07:36.489 --> 00:07:38.321
NICK: What time
did practice end?

83
00:07:38.458 --> 00:07:39.824
A little after 10:00.

84
00:07:39.893 --> 00:07:41.173
HANK: Did Lawson leave with you?

85
00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:43.763
No. He always stays to close up.

86
00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:45.350
Did anybody see him
leave the building?

87
00:07:45.865 --> 00:07:47.743
HANK: Did any of you see
anything strange when you left?

88
00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:48.928
Anything unusual?

89
00:07:49.035 --> 00:07:51.163
Maybe a car you
hadn't seen before?

90
00:07:51.237 --> 00:07:52.237
Somebody standing around?

91
00:07:52.439 --> 00:07:53.749
We just went to
our cars and left.

92
00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:55.765
It was late. so we
had to get home.

93
00:07:56.009 --> 00:07:57.068
We still had homework.

94
00:07:57.177 --> 00:07:59.772
Did Dr. Lawson seem a
little nervous last night?

95
00:07:59.846 --> 00:08:01.576
Maybe a little upset?

96
00:08:01.648 --> 00:08:03.549
SARAH: Yes. but that was. um...

97
00:08:04.451 --> 00:08:05.749
That was just Dr. Lawson.

98
00:08:05.819 --> 00:08:08.687
We found some cages in
the brush near the parking lot.

99
00:08:08.788 --> 00:08:11.033
Did you see anybody near
there when you left for your cars?

100
00:08:11.057 --> 00:08:12.218
What kind of cages?

101
00:08:12.292 --> 00:08:13.521
Used for trapping rodents.

102
00:08:14.894 --> 00:08:15.894
No.

103
00:08:19.366 --> 00:08:21.995
Well. if you can think
of anything else...

104
00:08:22.369 --> 00:08:24.031
Roddy Geiger went to our school.

105
00:08:24.904 --> 00:08:26.099
Who?

106
00:08:26.406 --> 00:08:27.499
His dad's an exterminator.

107
00:08:28.975 --> 00:08:30.466
Geiger Pest Control?

108
00:08:31.344 --> 00:08:32.368
Roddy wouldn't do this.

109
00:08:32.545 --> 00:08:34.138
Geiger's son goes
to your school.

110
00:08:34.347 --> 00:08:35.371
He did.

111
00:08:35.448 --> 00:08:36.973
He was suspended
a couple days ago.

112
00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:38.083
Why?

113
00:08:38.218 --> 00:08:39.516
If this is about that situation.

114
00:08:39.586 --> 00:08:41.953
maybe you'd better
speak to the school.

115
00:08:42.022 --> 00:08:43.102
That's a very troubled boy.

116
00:08:43.156 --> 00:08:45.556
I don't think it's appropriate
to talk to the kids about him.

117
00:08:58.271 --> 00:08:59.864
(VIOLIN PLAYING)

118
00:09:01.508 --> 00:09:02.635
Nice house.

119
00:09:02.709 --> 00:09:03.768
Yeah. Nice cars.

120
00:09:07.247 --> 00:09:08.909
Nice music.

121
00:09:09.049 --> 00:09:10.312
It's coming from over there.

122
00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:44.845
Captivated audience.

123
00:09:51.191 --> 00:09:52.191
Roddy Geiger?

124
00:09:52.425 --> 00:09:53.425
Yeah?

125
00:09:53.493 --> 00:09:55.894
I'm Detective Burkhardt.
this is Detective Griffin.

126
00:09:56.029 --> 00:09:57.361
You're pretty
good on that violin.

127
00:09:57.497 --> 00:09:59.577
What do you want? We want
to ask you a few questions.

128
00:10:00.567 --> 00:10:01.567
You cops?

129
00:10:01.901 --> 00:10:03.101
Well. we've been called worse.

130
00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:05.836
What do you want here?
Are you Mr. Geiger?

131
00:10:06.139 --> 00:10:08.199
You're here about that
teacher dying. aren't you?

132
00:10:08.274 --> 00:10:09.274
I heard all about it.

133
00:10:09.742 --> 00:10:11.176
Well. we had
nothing to do with it.

134
00:10:11.277 --> 00:10:12.788
Take it easy. sir. We just
want to ask a few questions.

135
00:10:12.812 --> 00:10:13.836
Who died?

136
00:10:13.913 --> 00:10:16.144
Dr. Lawson was found
dead in his car this morning.

137
00:10:16.683 --> 00:10:17.683
What?

138
00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.929
You don't talk to them until I
find out what they're going to do.

139
00:10:19.953 --> 00:10:21.097
What are you going
to do. arrest us?

140
00:10:21.121 --> 00:10:22.798
You going to arrest me?
You're going to arrest my boy?

141
00:10:22.822 --> 00:10:24.347
Sir. you need to calm down.

142
00:10:24.424 --> 00:10:27.155
Don't tell me to calm down.
I know what's going on here.

143
00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:29.071
They're trying to blame us
for what happened up there.

144
00:10:29.095 --> 00:10:30.706
and I'm tired of them
treating us like garbage.

145
00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:32.490
Stop. Don't move. Take
your hands off of him.

146
00:10:33.032 --> 00:10:34.056
Leave him alone.

147
00:10:35.435 --> 00:10:36.435
Leave him alone!

148
00:10:39.639 --> 00:10:41.359
Stop resisting! You're
only making it worse.

149
00:10:41.875 --> 00:10:43.571
I got him.

150
00:10:59.726 --> 00:11:00.853
(BOTH GRUNTING)

151
00:11:03.163 --> 00:11:04.683
I don't want to hurt
you. Yeah. you do.

152
00:11:04.898 --> 00:11:06.799
You're a Grimm.
You want to kill me.

153
00:11:13.373 --> 00:11:14.413
I'm not going to kill you.

154
00:11:15.275 --> 00:11:18.245
But you keep this up...
You're going to get hurt.

155
00:11:23.049 --> 00:11:27.145
Assaulting an officer. resisting
arrest hasn't made this any better.

156
00:11:27.554 --> 00:11:30.581
Now you might think
about a little cooperation.

157
00:11:32.425 --> 00:11:33.984
Where were you last night?

158
00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:35.289
Up in the mountains.

159
00:11:35.395 --> 00:11:37.193
A lot of mountains around here.

160
00:11:37.263 --> 00:11:39.255
Off Highway 26. past Sandy.

161
00:11:39.332 --> 00:11:40.332
What were you doing?

162
00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:42.562
I catch rats for a living.

163
00:11:42.635 --> 00:11:44.035
I don't kill 'em
if I don't have to.

164
00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:45.247
I turn the healthy ones loose.

165
00:11:45.271 --> 00:11:47.365
Can anyone testify to that? No.

166
00:11:47.473 --> 00:11:48.584
Where was your son last night?

167
00:11:48.608 --> 00:11:50.509
Home. Anybody home with him?

168
00:11:51.411 --> 00:11:52.411
<i>No.</i>

169
00:11:52.779 --> 00:11:54.890
You can kind of see the problem
we're faced with here. can't you?

170
00:11:54.914 --> 00:11:57.247
We had nothing to do
with that teacher dying.

171
00:11:57.317 --> 00:11:58.910
Your son was
suspended for fighting.

172
00:11:59.085 --> 00:12:01.179
Didn't that make you mad?

173
00:12:01.254 --> 00:12:03.018
If it were me. I
think I'd be mad.

174
00:12:03.089 --> 00:12:04.489
Don't try to understand me.

175
00:12:04.557 --> 00:12:06.719
How do you explain the
cages being up at the school?

176
00:12:06.793 --> 00:12:08.591
They were stolen two nights ago.

177
00:12:08.661 --> 00:12:10.061
HANK: <i>You report it?</i>

178
00:12:10.196 --> 00:12:14.964
<i>Yeah. sure. How many cops do
you think they put on stolen rat cages?</i>

179
00:12:16.169 --> 00:12:18.400
Those kids at that school
know what I do for a living.

180
00:12:18.571 --> 00:12:21.097
and they never
let Roddy forget it.

181
00:12:22.775 --> 00:12:24.038
You know. my boy's a prodigy.

182
00:12:24.611 --> 00:12:25.821
Better than anyone
at that school.

183
00:12:25.845 --> 00:12:27.541
Better than anyone in this city.

184
00:12:27.614 --> 00:12:29.446
But that didn't matter
because of what I do.

185
00:12:29.649 --> 00:12:32.016
What kind of relationship did
Roddy have with the teacher?

186
00:12:32.118 --> 00:12:33.118
Roddy didn't need him.

187
00:12:33.286 --> 00:12:34.549
And he let Dr. Lawson know it?

188
00:12:34.621 --> 00:12:35.816
He couldn't hide the obvious.

189
00:12:35.888 --> 00:12:38.653
Maybe Roddy snapped last night.

190
00:12:40.293 --> 00:12:41.784
What was the fight
at school about?

191
00:12:41.894 --> 00:12:43.419
They don't like me.
I don't like them.

192
00:12:43.529 --> 00:12:45.007
Yeah. well. you
don't hide it very well.

193
00:12:45.031 --> 00:12:47.091
Don't I? Really? That's so sad.

194
00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:53.496
Look. I get it.

195
00:12:54.073 --> 00:12:56.668
You're the outsider. No one
understands the world the way you do.

196
00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:59.372
Maybe you shouldn't
expect them to.

197
00:12:59.812 --> 00:13:01.576
I certainly don't
expect a Grimm to.

198
00:13:01.848 --> 00:13:02.848
Do you know many Grimms?

199
00:13:03.449 --> 00:13:04.449
I don't need to.

200
00:13:04.517 --> 00:13:06.452
Okay. so you know all about me

201
00:13:06.819 --> 00:13:08.530
because you've heard a
bunch of stories about me.

202
00:13:08.554 --> 00:13:10.154
and you know everything
you need to know.

203
00:13:10.556 --> 00:13:12.821
So if I asked these
kids at school.

204
00:13:12.892 --> 00:13:14.370
they'd tell me everything
I need to know.

205
00:13:14.394 --> 00:13:15.589
and it'd all be true. right?

206
00:13:15.662 --> 00:13:16.872
Just because they don't know me.

207
00:13:16.896 --> 00:13:18.096
that doesn't mean that you do.

208
00:13:18.865 --> 00:13:20.163
According to school records.

209
00:13:20.233 --> 00:13:23.499
Dr. Lawson reported you for attacking
Carter Brimley and Trey Harrison.

210
00:13:23.736 --> 00:13:25.705
Yeah. I attacked them
after they jumped me.

211
00:13:25.772 --> 00:13:27.434
According to Marvin... Marvin?

212
00:13:27.674 --> 00:13:30.041
Their little butter-boy?
'Cause he wouldn't lie.

213
00:13:30.209 --> 00:13:31.920
Maybe this thing didn't turn
out the way you planned.

214
00:13:31.944 --> 00:13:34.072
Maybe you were just
trying to scare your teacher.

215
00:13:34.147 --> 00:13:35.513
I wasn't there last night.

216
00:13:35.615 --> 00:13:36.615
Where were you?

217
00:13:37.583 --> 00:13:38.607
I was at a rave.

218
00:13:38.685 --> 00:13:39.685
Where?

219
00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:41.547
Down by the river.

220
00:13:41.621 --> 00:13:42.645
Be more specific.

221
00:13:43.823 --> 00:13:45.655
It's an old building
on Front Street.

222
00:13:45.792 --> 00:13:46.816
Anybody there with you?

223
00:13:47.093 --> 00:13:48.213
Only about a couple hundred.

224
00:13:48.328 --> 00:13:49.819
Could any of them identify you?

225
00:13:50.863 --> 00:13:51.863
One.

226
00:13:51.998 --> 00:13:52.998
Got a name?

227
00:13:53.232 --> 00:13:55.497
So you can arrest him for
putting on an illegal rave?

228
00:13:55.568 --> 00:13:57.503
Yeah. That's my dream.

229
00:13:58.571 --> 00:14:00.972
Look. you either prove to
me where you were last night.

230
00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:03.202
or you go to jail.

231
00:14:05.445 --> 00:14:06.622
WU: You're never
going to believe this.

232
00:14:06.646 --> 00:14:08.486
I talked to Sammy. the
guy who put on the rave.

233
00:14:09.148 --> 00:14:11.379
Your perp is DJ Retchid Kat.

234
00:14:12.452 --> 00:14:13.681
Who's DJ Retchid Kat?

235
00:14:13.853 --> 00:14:15.515
Tell me you know.
Of course I know.

236
00:14:15.788 --> 00:14:17.984
Everybody knows.
Who's DJ Retchid Kat?

237
00:14:19.125 --> 00:14:21.390
Only the most famous
raver in Portland.

238
00:14:21.794 --> 00:14:24.006
Not that men of your age would
know what I'm talking about.

239
00:14:24.030 --> 00:14:25.054
You didn't know either.

240
00:14:25.164 --> 00:14:26.325
Not until I talked to Sammy.

241
00:14:26.432 --> 00:14:28.924
DJ Retchid Kat always
wears a big cat head.

242
00:14:29.035 --> 00:14:30.936
and Sammy is the only
one who knows who he is.

243
00:14:31.003 --> 00:14:32.437
and he swears it is your guy.

244
00:14:32.572 --> 00:14:34.507
So his alibi's good.
But not his dad's.

245
00:14:34.707 --> 00:14:36.667
Except why would he leave
his cages at the school?

246
00:14:36.776 --> 00:14:39.376
Not so clever. Unless he wanted
us to believe somebody stole them.

247
00:14:39.846 --> 00:14:40.870
Then it's clever.

248
00:14:42.115 --> 00:14:43.743
Let Roddy go. hold onto the dad?

249
00:14:43.816 --> 00:14:44.943
Absolutely.

250
00:14:45.051 --> 00:14:47.316
Not to mention. he
assaulted an officer.

251
00:14:47.387 --> 00:14:49.481
He deserves a little
downtime for that alone.

252
00:14:53.559 --> 00:14:54.559
You're free to go.

253
00:14:54.827 --> 00:14:55.827
What about my dad?

254
00:14:55.928 --> 00:14:57.521
Not until we verify his alibi.

255
00:14:58.998 --> 00:15:00.967
You know he can't do that.

256
00:15:06.072 --> 00:15:07.506
Pretty excited
about being let go.

257
00:15:07.707 --> 00:15:09.573
Oh. yeah. I had to
stop him from yodeling.

258
00:15:11.277 --> 00:15:13.746
Harper called. Dead
guy wants to see us.

259
00:15:14.213 --> 00:15:15.704
He died of a heart attack.

260
00:15:15.882 --> 00:15:17.214
So the rats scared him to death?

261
00:15:17.617 --> 00:15:18.915
Well. they didn't help.

262
00:15:18.985 --> 00:15:22.217
But he was on digoxin and
angiotensin for his heart.

263
00:15:22.455 --> 00:15:24.215
He was kind of high
up on death's to-do list.

264
00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:26.201
So the rats were put
in the car to kill him.

265
00:15:26.225 --> 00:15:27.523
If they knew
about his condition.

266
00:15:27.627 --> 00:15:30.147
But no guarantee a scare like
that would trigger a heart attack.

267
00:15:30.596 --> 00:15:32.724
Prank gone bad.
Yeah. or a threat.

268
00:15:33.533 --> 00:15:34.899
Then it's probably Roddy's dad.

269
00:15:35.001 --> 00:15:36.245
A homicide occurred
in the course

270
00:15:36.269 --> 00:15:38.747
of an intentional maiming of the
victim. so it's aggravated murder.

271
00:15:38.771 --> 00:15:41.240
I did find something
interesting in my other autopsy.

272
00:15:41.941 --> 00:15:43.136
What other autopsy?

273
00:15:48.714 --> 00:15:49.943
Oh. man.

274
00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:52.776
There goes lunch.
Well. speaking of...

275
00:15:53.085 --> 00:15:55.645
A rat's stomach is like a road
map to where they've been.

276
00:15:55.922 --> 00:15:58.016
Here we have some
undigested bits of your victim.

277
00:15:58.758 --> 00:16:01.819
and some colored
cloth and nylon fibers

278
00:16:02.295 --> 00:16:04.335
that didn't match any of
the clothes he was wearing.

279
00:16:05.064 --> 00:16:07.260
They were chewing on
something else in the car?

280
00:16:07.333 --> 00:16:09.564
Probably before
Dr. Lawson got in.

281
00:16:10.269 --> 00:16:11.269
Take a look at this.

282
00:16:11.337 --> 00:16:12.930
Oh. do I have to?

283
00:16:14.674 --> 00:16:16.040
It's green and red.

284
00:16:17.043 --> 00:16:18.636
Same colors as the music school.

285
00:16:18.878 --> 00:16:21.040
Let's find out if it matches
anything in Lawson's car.

286
00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:32.752
"Rats dine on beloved teacher."

287
00:16:33.092 --> 00:16:35.152
That's a little cold. Guess
who came to dinner?

288
00:16:35.328 --> 00:16:37.490
What do you got on this?
Press wants a statement.

289
00:16:37.563 --> 00:16:39.828
We have one suspect in
custody. Has he been charged?

290
00:16:39.999 --> 00:16:42.010
We have enough evidence.
but we're not sure he's our guy.

291
00:16:42.034 --> 00:16:43.468
We're waiting on
some lab results.

292
00:16:43.536 --> 00:16:46.114
Well. I got a dead popular teacher
at an expensive private school.

293
00:16:46.138 --> 00:16:48.138
I'd like an answer before
politics screw things up.

294
00:17:16.035 --> 00:17:18.195
What are you doing here?
The cops just arrested my dad.

295
00:17:18.271 --> 00:17:19.271
What?

296
00:17:19.438 --> 00:17:21.116
Whoever did this wanted
them to think it was him.

297
00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:22.140
Or me.

298
00:17:23.509 --> 00:17:24.841
That's what everybody thinks.

299
00:17:24.911 --> 00:17:26.174
You think it was me?

300
00:17:26.512 --> 00:17:27.912
You were the one
that got suspended.

301
00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:30.074
That was bogus. I
thought you knew that.

302
00:17:30.149 --> 00:17:31.549
Why didn't you say anything?

303
00:17:32.818 --> 00:17:33.911
They're my friends.

304
00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:35.744
And I'm what?

305
00:17:38.357 --> 00:17:40.155
Someone I used to care about.

306
00:17:40.426 --> 00:17:41.485
Used to?

307
00:17:43.529 --> 00:17:44.529
Roddy...

308
00:17:44.597 --> 00:17:45.860
So now you're with Carter?

309
00:17:55.708 --> 00:17:57.370
I can't do this.
You still love me.

310
00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:59.342
I can't keep sneaking
out to be with you.

311
00:18:01.514 --> 00:18:03.714
And if you didn't put the
rats in his car. then who did?

312
00:18:03.849 --> 00:18:04.849
Your boyfriend.

313
00:18:05.384 --> 00:18:06.511
He would not do that.

314
00:18:06.586 --> 00:18:08.782
Yeah. he would.

315
00:18:08.854 --> 00:18:10.379
To get to you.
and get rid of me.

316
00:18:11.157 --> 00:18:12.489
What are you doing here?

317
00:18:12.558 --> 00:18:14.169
I thought that this was
over and done with.

318
00:18:14.193 --> 00:18:15.889
Your father will go ballistic.

319
00:18:16.028 --> 00:18:17.656
Please go get in the house.

320
00:18:20.232 --> 00:18:21.461
Stay away from my daughter.

321
00:18:22.034 --> 00:18:23.593
Stay away from my family.

322
00:18:31.477 --> 00:18:33.446
What are you
doing here. rat-boy?

323
00:18:33.546 --> 00:18:35.139
Ah. ah. ah. ah. ah.

324
00:18:37.083 --> 00:18:38.415
Come on. Do it.

325
00:18:38.751 --> 00:18:40.831
I wonder what the police
will say when they get here.

326
00:18:40.953 --> 00:18:42.182
You're going to pay.

327
00:18:42.722 --> 00:18:44.350
Some of us can afford to.

328
00:18:45.758 --> 00:18:46.758
(THUDS)

329
00:18:51.897 --> 00:18:53.126
The investigation is ongoing.

330
00:18:53.933 --> 00:18:55.444
Because of the unusual
nature of the death.

331
00:18:55.468 --> 00:18:59.132
we are taking extra measures to make
sure that nothing has been overlooked.

332
00:19:00.373 --> 00:19:02.672
Dr. Lawson was an important
member of our community.

333
00:19:02.742 --> 00:19:05.439
and. uh. an inspiration
to a lot of young people.

334
00:19:06.045 --> 00:19:08.207
His untimely death has
caused a great deal of distress.

335
00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:09.992
and I promise that
every effort will be made

336
00:19:10.016 --> 00:19:12.815
to bring the person or
persons responsible to justice.

337
00:19:14.220 --> 00:19:15.381
I'll take your questions now.

338
00:19:15.921 --> 00:19:17.412
Preliminary lab
reports just came in

339
00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:19.186
on the fibers found
in the rat's stomach.

340
00:19:19.258 --> 00:19:22.160
Some of them were nylon.
the kind found in car carpeting.

341
00:19:22.228 --> 00:19:24.527
BMW. Audi. Porsche.

342
00:19:24.597 --> 00:19:26.725
You know. the kind of
vehicles we don't drive.

343
00:19:26.799 --> 00:19:28.062
And neither do the Geigers.

344
00:19:28.134 --> 00:19:29.796
The colored fibers
are from blankets.

345
00:19:30.169 --> 00:19:32.695
There's a Mrs. Jessup
here demanding to see you.

346
00:19:33.305 --> 00:19:35.672
She's got. uh...
How can I say this?

347
00:19:36.375 --> 00:19:38.867
Smoke coming out
of a lot of orifices.

348
00:19:41.147 --> 00:19:42.479
Good luck.

349
00:19:43.182 --> 00:19:45.310
Why hasn't Roddy
Geiger been arrested?

350
00:19:45.685 --> 00:19:48.120
He came to my house and
he harassed my daughter.

351
00:19:48.287 --> 00:19:49.653
This boy is out of control.

352
00:19:49.722 --> 00:19:51.366
He got himself thrown
out of school for fighting...

353
00:19:51.390 --> 00:19:53.882
We can't arrest Roddy Geiger
or anybody without evidence.

354
00:19:53.959 --> 00:19:56.827
Well. then get some
before somebody else dies.

355
00:19:56.962 --> 00:19:59.022
I do not want him
coming to my house.

356
00:19:59.165 --> 00:20:00.428
Why is he coming to your house?

357
00:20:00.499 --> 00:20:02.400
My daughter went out
with him a couple of times.

358
00:20:02.501 --> 00:20:03.992
Now he thinks he owns her.

359
00:20:04.170 --> 00:20:07.231
If my husband sees him
again. I'm afraid of what he'll do.

360
00:20:07.873 --> 00:20:09.842
That boy does not
belong in our school.

361
00:20:09.909 --> 00:20:11.070
Or in your neighborhood?

362
00:20:13.112 --> 00:20:14.478
Shouldn't you be
writing this down?

363
00:20:15.281 --> 00:20:17.147
I am filing a report. aren't I?

364
00:20:20.886 --> 00:20:21.966
I haven't had that much fun

365
00:20:22.021 --> 00:20:24.166
since that drunk threw up
on me at the Christmas party.

366
00:20:24.190 --> 00:20:25.658
Wasn't that Sergeant Wu?

367
00:20:25.725 --> 00:20:28.024
It was. and I'm meeting
him at Clark Lewis for a drink.

368
00:20:28.094 --> 00:20:29.653
Want to go?

369
00:20:29.729 --> 00:20:30.753
Don't answer.

370
00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:33.493
You've got Juliette.
you're in love. you got a life.

371
00:20:34.066 --> 00:20:35.466
Go live it. my child.

372
00:20:35.534 --> 00:20:37.614
Leave alcohol to those of
us who are still searching.

373
00:20:39.071 --> 00:20:40.505
Reinigen?

374
00:20:40.573 --> 00:20:42.269
They're bottom of
the food chain. man.

375
00:20:42.408 --> 00:20:44.900
Let me tell ya. the
food in their chain?

376
00:20:45.111 --> 00:20:46.807
Gourmet is not their forte.

377
00:20:46.879 --> 00:20:49.678
But they're rarely violent unless
they're pushed to the limit. right?

378
00:20:49.882 --> 00:20:51.145
Correct.

379
00:20:51.817 --> 00:20:53.428
If you know all that.
what are you doing here?

380
00:20:53.452 --> 00:20:54.930
How would you feel
about talking to a...

381
00:20:54.954 --> 00:20:56.047
Reinigen?

382
00:20:58.491 --> 00:21:00.926
I'm not protecting
anyone for you. am I?

383
00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:02.651
Last time I protected
someone for you

384
00:21:02.795 --> 00:21:04.696
was not exactly a
pleasant experience.

385
00:21:04.764 --> 00:21:05.925
How is that guy. by the way?

386
00:21:06.031 --> 00:21:07.375
Were they able to
sew his arm back on?

387
00:21:07.399 --> 00:21:10.079
Uh. I don't think he's going to be
beating anybody up with it again.

388
00:21:13.072 --> 00:21:15.667
Look. you like music.
right? I mean. you play.

389
00:21:15.841 --> 00:21:17.036
I don't do parties.

390
00:21:17.109 --> 00:21:18.805
This kid. he is
pretty incredible.

391
00:21:18.978 --> 00:21:20.606
At what? Violin.

392
00:21:21.547 --> 00:21:23.778
He got a scholarship to
the Von Hamelin Institute.

393
00:21:23.983 --> 00:21:26.817
Is this about that teacher
who wound up as ratatouille?

394
00:21:26.886 --> 00:21:29.219
Okay. some people think
he was involved. I don't.

395
00:21:30.289 --> 00:21:31.587
This kid is a stick of dynamite.

396
00:21:31.657 --> 00:21:33.250
He knows I'm a Grimm. And a cop.

397
00:21:33.425 --> 00:21:35.394
So he's not exactly
open to... Yeah. yeah.

398
00:21:35.461 --> 00:21:36.986
A heart to heart.
I got the picture.

399
00:21:37.663 --> 00:21:40.189
You think he'll listen to
me 'cause I play the cello?

400
00:21:40.499 --> 00:21:43.162
Just so you know.
Reinigen and Blutbaden

401
00:21:43.235 --> 00:21:44.430
are not drinking buddies.

402
00:21:49.909 --> 00:21:52.208
I've never been much
of a do-gooder. Nick.

403
00:21:52.578 --> 00:21:56.447
The only bleeding
heart I ever had was a...

404
00:21:56.515 --> 00:21:58.541
I mean. that's in the
past. I'm just saying.

405
00:21:58.818 --> 00:22:00.095
Look. I was
different growing up.

406
00:22:00.119 --> 00:22:01.644
and I have a feeling
you were. too.

407
00:22:03.155 --> 00:22:05.522
Monroe. this kid just
needs a little bit of help.

408
00:22:08.727 --> 00:22:10.025
He's not a rapper. is he?

409
00:22:10.129 --> 00:22:12.792
I mean. nothing against
rappers. it's just. you know...

410
00:22:14.466 --> 00:22:16.765
Where's the melody?

411
00:22:22.341 --> 00:22:24.867
BUD: (GROANS) Damn it!

412
00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:27.639
(GROANS) I can't get
this damn screw loose.

413
00:22:32.117 --> 00:22:33.608
How long has this been going on?

414
00:22:33.686 --> 00:22:35.348
Oh. since 4:30. I'm sorry.

415
00:22:35.421 --> 00:22:36.719
I'm going as fast as I can.

416
00:22:36.822 --> 00:22:38.051
Will you be done tonight?

417
00:22:38.157 --> 00:22:39.801
What. do you think
I'm going to sleep here?

418
00:22:39.825 --> 00:22:41.726
Aw. crap! I cut my hand.

419
00:22:41.861 --> 00:22:43.659
Ooh. I'll get a bandage.

420
00:22:44.063 --> 00:22:46.362
I hate this model.
It's a deathtrap.

421
00:22:47.099 --> 00:22:48.829
Look. it's trying to kill me.

422
00:22:55.808 --> 00:22:58.573
(NERVOUSLY) Please.
please. don't. don't hurt me.

423
00:22:59.011 --> 00:23:00.843
Oh. God. Oh. please!

424
00:23:03.782 --> 00:23:05.250
What happened? What did you do?

425
00:23:05.551 --> 00:23:07.417
Nothing. He just ran out?

426
00:23:07.486 --> 00:23:09.819
It looked like he
was terrified of you.

427
00:23:09.922 --> 00:23:11.288
Yeah. I know.

428
00:23:12.224 --> 00:23:14.455
Well. that's really
weird. isn't it. Nick?

429
00:23:14.627 --> 00:23:16.118
Maybe it was the refrigerator.

430
00:23:16.195 --> 00:23:18.061
You know. he said it
was trying to kill him.

431
00:23:18.130 --> 00:23:19.496
Well. now what do we do?

432
00:23:19.765 --> 00:23:20.994
Go out.

433
00:23:21.333 --> 00:23:23.768
I'm telling you. he's got
an instinct for people.

434
00:23:24.536 --> 00:23:26.664
Most of the time. he's right.

435
00:23:27.606 --> 00:23:29.084
Well. it's too bad Nick
wasn't your partner

436
00:23:29.108 --> 00:23:30.667
when you met your last wife.

437
00:23:30.876 --> 00:23:33.573
That's cold. You got to
learn to say no to temptation.

438
00:23:35.247 --> 00:23:36.772
Hey. how 'bout some dinner?

439
00:23:38.017 --> 00:23:39.508
I'm tempted. but no.

440
00:23:39.752 --> 00:23:42.586
I've got a big day tomorrow.
I've got to get some sleep.

441
00:23:43.756 --> 00:23:45.418
So you're paying. right?

442
00:23:51.063 --> 00:23:52.156
I'll see you tomorrow.

443
00:23:52.598 --> 00:23:55.227
(CHUCKLES) Hey. Bill. Yeah?

444
00:23:56.235 --> 00:23:57.965
Lonely Sergeant
needs a steak over here.

445
00:24:01.106 --> 00:24:03.041
Yeah. next week
will be fine. Okay.

446
00:24:05.744 --> 00:24:08.077
Hey. Miss Schade. right?

447
00:24:08.280 --> 00:24:09.680
Detective... Griffin.

448
00:24:09.782 --> 00:24:11.250
Hank. That's right.

449
00:24:11.717 --> 00:24:13.481
Sorry. I should've
remembered that.

450
00:24:13.886 --> 00:24:15.286
You saved my life.

451
00:24:17.623 --> 00:24:18.682
So how have you been?

452
00:24:19.091 --> 00:24:20.889
Busy. How've you been?

453
00:24:21.593 --> 00:24:24.028
Busy. Which is good right now.

454
00:24:26.065 --> 00:24:28.694
Well. you take care. You. too.

455
00:24:29.335 --> 00:24:30.564
Hey. Hank?

456
00:24:31.837 --> 00:24:33.897
I don't suppose you'd
want to save me again.

457
00:24:36.809 --> 00:24:37.868
From what?

458
00:24:37.943 --> 00:24:39.969
My business meeting canceled.

459
00:24:40.245 --> 00:24:44.046
and I've got this great
table. an empty chair.

460
00:24:45.050 --> 00:24:46.712
Maybe it's time
for a little payback.

461
00:24:47.820 --> 00:24:49.118
Can I buy you dinner?

462
00:24:52.791 --> 00:24:54.817
Yeah. sure. Sounds great.

463
00:25:05.037 --> 00:25:06.665
(VIOLIN PLAYING)

464
00:25:51.016 --> 00:25:52.541
(KNOCKING AT DOOR)

465
00:25:59.324 --> 00:26:02.294
You were kicking some butt
on that Brahms concerto. man.

466
00:26:02.394 --> 00:26:04.454
It was brilliantly executed.

467
00:26:04.563 --> 00:26:05.690
Very fluid.

468
00:26:06.899 --> 00:26:07.992
Who are you?

469
00:26:08.067 --> 00:26:10.059
Monroe. We don't
know each other.

470
00:26:10.135 --> 00:26:11.728
I'm a friend of
Detective Burkhardt's.

471
00:26:12.404 --> 00:26:14.339
No. thanks. Uh-uh.

472
00:26:16.842 --> 00:26:18.470
I wasn't finished.

473
00:26:20.512 --> 00:26:23.243
Now. I don't normally
do this kind of thing.

474
00:26:23.315 --> 00:26:25.409
but we both know who Nick is.

475
00:26:25.884 --> 00:26:28.376
And he is not like the other
ones we've heard about.

476
00:26:29.088 --> 00:26:30.088
<i>Capisce?</i>

477
00:26:30.923 --> 00:26:32.824
Believe it or not. he's
worried about you.

478
00:26:34.026 --> 00:26:35.466
And he knew you
wouldn't talk to him.

479
00:26:35.527 --> 00:26:37.127
so he thought maybe
you would talk to me.

480
00:26:37.596 --> 00:26:40.031
About what? About
not being stupid.

481
00:26:40.899 --> 00:26:43.266
He said you had
talent. man. and it's true.

482
00:26:43.569 --> 00:26:44.628
I just heard it.

483
00:26:44.937 --> 00:26:46.633
And I've been
around a lot of people

484
00:26:46.805 --> 00:26:48.137
who thought they had talent.

485
00:26:48.207 --> 00:26:50.676
Yours truly is one of them.
But the real thing. man.

486
00:26:51.043 --> 00:26:52.944
The real thing is
an impossibility.

487
00:26:53.045 --> 00:26:54.823
You don't know where it
comes from. or what made it.

488
00:26:54.847 --> 00:26:57.510
but it's one of the mysteries
of life that lifts us all

489
00:26:57.583 --> 00:26:59.575
out of the misery of average.

490
00:26:59.852 --> 00:27:02.583
And one of the problems
is you people who have it

491
00:27:02.721 --> 00:27:04.747
don't think it's any big deal.

492
00:27:04.890 --> 00:27:06.415
That just pisses me off.

493
00:27:07.526 --> 00:27:10.826
So the bottom line is
you don't throw that away.

494
00:27:16.268 --> 00:27:17.395
Is this going well?

495
00:27:17.469 --> 00:27:20.069
I mean. I feel like it should be
a little more back and forth. no?

496
00:27:20.405 --> 00:27:21.429
I don't know.

497
00:27:22.307 --> 00:27:23.673
Yeah. you do.

498
00:27:25.144 --> 00:27:27.584
Just 'cause you're young. doesn't
mean you're smarter than me.

499
00:27:30.182 --> 00:27:31.514
Okay? So...

500
00:27:33.218 --> 00:27:36.950
Basically what we're saying
here is. uh. just don't blow it.

501
00:27:37.990 --> 00:27:39.788
Man. I'm tired.

502
00:27:41.193 --> 00:27:45.255
I'm not used to this intimate
one-on-one thing. you know?

503
00:27:47.432 --> 00:27:49.110
I know you're probably
kind of weirded out.

504
00:27:49.134 --> 00:27:51.160
a Reinigen getting
advice from a Blutbad.

505
00:27:51.303 --> 00:27:54.296
It doesn't ever really
happen. but listen to me.

506
00:27:54.873 --> 00:28:00.938
Sometimes our lives collide
in the most bizarre ways.

507
00:28:02.314 --> 00:28:03.543
Right?

508
00:28:06.485 --> 00:28:08.181
Still nothing? Okay.

509
00:28:09.221 --> 00:28:11.247
Well. you know
what I'm saying. right?

510
00:28:11.323 --> 00:28:13.087
Take care. And if you
ever need anything...

511
00:28:18.063 --> 00:28:19.258
Call me.

512
00:28:21.934 --> 00:28:23.300
All right.

513
00:28:24.369 --> 00:28:25.632
(TELEPHONE RINGING)

514
00:28:28.540 --> 00:28:31.009
Hello? <i>This is Officer
Clay from Central Jail.</i>

515
00:28:31.176 --> 00:28:32.974
<i>Is this Roddy Geiger?</i> Yeah.

516
00:28:33.045 --> 00:28:35.173
<i>I have to inform you.
your father was injured</i>

517
00:28:35.247 --> 00:28:37.239
<i>when he refused
to enter his cell.</i>

518
00:28:37.449 --> 00:28:38.449
Is he okay?

519
00:28:38.517 --> 00:28:40.110
<i>He's being treated
in the infirmary.</i>

520
00:28:40.385 --> 00:28:43.480
<i>He's got a concussion.
No visitors for 48 hours.</i>

521
00:28:48.060 --> 00:28:49.585
Maybe you arrested him once.

522
00:28:49.795 --> 00:28:51.787
Who? The refrigerator repairman.

523
00:28:51.863 --> 00:28:53.525
Maybe that's why
he was so upset.

524
00:28:53.665 --> 00:28:55.258
Right. Yeah.

525
00:28:55.334 --> 00:28:57.462
I didn't even think of that.

526
00:28:57.569 --> 00:28:59.299
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

527
00:29:01.473 --> 00:29:02.566
Burkhardt.

528
00:29:02.641 --> 00:29:05.577
Hey. so I talked to
Roddy. The Reinigen kid?

529
00:29:05.644 --> 00:29:08.580
And I don't want to
toot my own horn here.

530
00:29:08.647 --> 00:29:10.548
but I think I made some inroads.

531
00:29:10.649 --> 00:29:12.174
<i>Gave him a lot to think about.</i>

532
00:29:12.284 --> 00:29:13.461
Well. thanks. I appreciate it.

533
00:29:13.485 --> 00:29:15.147
No problem at all.

534
00:29:15.287 --> 00:29:18.086
I think that kid's going to be
on a little different tack now.

535
00:29:18.824 --> 00:29:19.985
(TECHNO MUSIC PLAYING)

536
00:29:21.493 --> 00:29:22.825
(RODDY YELLING)

537
00:29:35.240 --> 00:29:37.040
Once we got confirmation
that the nylon fibers

538
00:29:37.142 --> 00:29:39.111
in the rat's stomach
were used in German cars.

539
00:29:39.177 --> 00:29:40.577
we ruled out the teacher's car.

540
00:29:40.712 --> 00:29:42.408
We ran every
student registration

541
00:29:42.514 --> 00:29:45.460
at the Von Hamelin Institute to see if
we could find a match with the fibers.

542
00:29:45.484 --> 00:29:47.564
I'm guessing half the student
body drive German cars.

543
00:29:47.619 --> 00:29:50.282
Actually we narrowed it
down to just BMWs and Audis

544
00:29:50.355 --> 00:29:52.085
that use the nylon
we're looking for.

545
00:29:52.157 --> 00:29:54.092
But the style is
only used in SUVs.

546
00:29:54.293 --> 00:29:56.694
We clicked it down from
there to a half-dozen students.

547
00:29:56.795 --> 00:30:00.061
One of them had a fight
with Roddy. Carter Brimley.

548
00:30:00.132 --> 00:30:03.660
And he drives a BMW X5.
which is a match with the fibers.

549
00:30:04.603 --> 00:30:05.603
Get a warrant.

550
00:30:05.937 --> 00:30:06.996
Yeah.

551
00:30:11.510 --> 00:30:13.411
(TECHNO MUSIC PLAYING)

552
00:30:55.487 --> 00:30:56.487
(CRASHES)

553
00:31:18.110 --> 00:31:19.134
Just talked to Sarah.

554
00:31:20.512 --> 00:31:22.023
Roddy came over to
her house yesterday.

555
00:31:22.047 --> 00:31:23.140
He knows we did it.

556
00:31:23.281 --> 00:31:25.273
Saying it and proving it
are two different things.

557
00:31:25.350 --> 00:31:26.682
She asked me if we did it.

558
00:31:27.319 --> 00:31:28.679
You weren't dumb
enough to say yes.

559
00:31:28.854 --> 00:31:31.289
No. but I'm a little
bit freaking out here.

560
00:31:31.390 --> 00:31:34.189
Everybody knows Roddy is
a lot better player than Carter.

561
00:31:34.326 --> 00:31:35.988
and the only reason
he got the chair

562
00:31:36.061 --> 00:31:38.541
is because we got him booted.
and so he could be next to Sarah.

563
00:31:39.164 --> 00:31:40.462
Grow some.

564
00:31:40.532 --> 00:31:43.092
Check it. DJ Retchid
Kat rave tonight.

565
00:31:43.402 --> 00:31:44.495
Awesome.

566
00:31:44.703 --> 00:31:45.898
(PHONE BEEPING) Oh.

567
00:31:46.905 --> 00:31:49.602
Are we going? Well. the men are.

568
00:31:49.741 --> 00:31:51.039
This is ridiculous.

569
00:31:51.109 --> 00:31:53.544
My son had nothing to do with
what happened to Dr. Lawson.

570
00:31:53.678 --> 00:31:55.203
That's what we're
here to find out.

571
00:31:55.280 --> 00:31:56.407
Then I should call a lawyer.

572
00:31:56.481 --> 00:31:57.813
Well. that's your
privilege. sir.

573
00:31:57.883 --> 00:31:59.527
but you'll still need
to open your son's car.

574
00:31:59.551 --> 00:32:01.179
Or we'll have to do it by force.

575
00:32:01.486 --> 00:32:04.479
This is great. This is
where my tax money goes.

576
00:32:05.056 --> 00:32:06.134
What do you think
you're going to find?

577
00:32:06.158 --> 00:32:07.490
There's nothing in there.

578
00:32:07.559 --> 00:32:08.652
That's what they all say.

579
00:32:11.830 --> 00:32:13.799
We got holes. Bag it.

580
00:32:14.232 --> 00:32:15.757
Holes? What does that mean?

581
00:32:16.034 --> 00:32:17.263
What do we have here?

582
00:32:20.939 --> 00:32:21.939
Not a chocolate chip.

583
00:32:22.073 --> 00:32:24.419
And the color of the carpeting
matches the fibers we've got.

584
00:32:24.443 --> 00:32:25.934
Sir. we're going to
impound your car.

585
00:32:26.044 --> 00:32:27.774
What? Tell us where your son is.

586
00:32:28.914 --> 00:32:31.074
I'm not saying anything
to you till I talk to a lawyer.

587
00:32:31.116 --> 00:32:33.261
Well. in that case. we'll have to
put a warrant out for his arrest.

588
00:32:33.285 --> 00:32:35.296
he'll be taken to Central
Jail... (CELL PHONE RINGING)

589
00:32:35.320 --> 00:32:37.448
Whoa. whoa. whoa. whoa.
he's just out with friends.

590
00:32:37.522 --> 00:32:38.649
Uh-huh. Who?

591
00:32:38.790 --> 00:32:40.452
He left with Trey
about an hour ago.

592
00:32:40.525 --> 00:32:41.602
They were going to see a movie.

593
00:32:41.626 --> 00:32:43.458
Nick. we got a fire
at the Geiger house.

594
00:32:44.229 --> 00:32:45.629
You got this? Yeah. got it. Go.

595
00:32:53.939 --> 00:32:55.237
Somebody let the dogs out.

596
00:32:55.307 --> 00:32:56.751
And I'm guessing it's
the same somebody

597
00:32:56.775 --> 00:32:58.368
who trashed Roddy's room.

598
00:32:58.443 --> 00:32:59.775
We'd better get
to Sarah's house.

599
00:33:00.679 --> 00:33:02.204
(TECHNO MUSIC PLAYING)

600
00:33:28.006 --> 00:33:29.286
We need to talk
to your daughter.

601
00:33:29.541 --> 00:33:31.442
Why? She hasn't done anything.

602
00:33:31.510 --> 00:33:33.590
We need to know where
she is. She might be in danger.

603
00:33:34.846 --> 00:33:36.280
She's with friends
at the movies.

604
00:33:36.348 --> 00:33:37.714
You need to call her.

605
00:33:37.849 --> 00:33:39.374
(PHONE DIALING)

606
00:33:43.622 --> 00:33:45.147
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

607
00:33:45.357 --> 00:33:47.417
She didn't take her phone.

608
00:33:53.098 --> 00:33:54.623
I think we got it.

609
00:33:54.733 --> 00:33:55.894
MAN: <i>The terror</i>

610
00:33:56.201 --> 00:33:57.669
(TECHNO MUSIC PLAYING)

611
00:34:08.580 --> 00:34:09.604
(VIOLIN PLAYING)

612
00:34:50.989 --> 00:34:52.548
Are we in the wrong place?

613
00:34:53.191 --> 00:34:54.523
We're the only ones here.

614
00:34:55.427 --> 00:34:56.907
Maybe we're not
supposed to park here.

615
00:34:57.028 --> 00:35:00.226
Who cares where we park?
It's started. I can hear it.

616
00:35:04.202 --> 00:35:05.329
What are you doing?

617
00:35:06.304 --> 00:35:07.966
Did you guys have
anything to do with it?

618
00:35:08.039 --> 00:35:09.371
What are you talking about?

619
00:35:09.574 --> 00:35:10.854
You know what I'm talking about.

620
00:35:11.676 --> 00:35:13.645
Are you crazy?
Come on. let's go.

621
00:35:13.712 --> 00:35:15.806
Did you get Roddy suspended?

622
00:35:16.414 --> 00:35:19.543
No. he jumped us. and
we just defended ourselves.

623
00:35:19.951 --> 00:35:22.614
What's the matter? You
want to be with rat-boy now?

624
00:35:22.687 --> 00:35:23.746
Shut up.

625
00:35:23.822 --> 00:35:25.462
Are you coming or
not? 'Cause we're going.

626
00:35:37.068 --> 00:35:39.003
(FAINT TECHNO MUSIC PLAYING)

627
00:35:41.172 --> 00:35:42.640
Where is it?

628
00:35:53.218 --> 00:35:54.550
It's coming from underground.

629
00:35:54.619 --> 00:35:56.281
Oh. man. that is so literal.

630
00:35:56.855 --> 00:35:58.483
Oh. this is so sick.

631
00:36:01.793 --> 00:36:03.386
I... I don't know if
we should do this.

632
00:36:03.561 --> 00:36:04.961
Ah. what's your problem?

633
00:36:05.096 --> 00:36:06.296
Come on. it's already started.

634
00:36:21.980 --> 00:36:23.539
My old man called three times.

635
00:36:23.682 --> 00:36:25.150
Yeah. mine did. too.

636
00:36:25.216 --> 00:36:27.048
(CHUCKLES) My
mom called four times.

637
00:36:27.485 --> 00:36:29.005
Dude. don't they
know we're at a movie?

638
00:36:40.231 --> 00:36:42.427
Yeah. that's Trey's
car. Plates match.

639
00:36:44.002 --> 00:36:45.282
Music's coming
from the building.

640
00:37:03.722 --> 00:37:05.213
(TECHNO MUSIC GETTING LOUDER)

641
00:37:09.527 --> 00:37:11.086
SARAH: Okay.
this is really weird.

642
00:37:11.796 --> 00:37:13.025
This way. Through here.

643
00:37:32.550 --> 00:37:34.018
(WHOOPING) Oh. man.

644
00:37:34.085 --> 00:37:35.348
This is tight! This is so cool.

645
00:37:36.488 --> 00:37:38.354
MARVIN: Check this place. y'all.

646
00:37:39.224 --> 00:37:40.419
(WHOOPING) Yeah!

647
00:37:41.259 --> 00:37:42.522
Yes! Yeah.

648
00:37:43.294 --> 00:37:44.353
SARAH: Sweet.

649
00:37:46.331 --> 00:37:47.458
We're the only ones here.

650
00:37:48.199 --> 00:37:49.565
Historical.

651
00:37:50.935 --> 00:37:52.801
SARAH: Oh. wow.
(MUSIC STOPS PLAYING)

652
00:37:53.104 --> 00:37:54.504
What the hell. man. We early?

653
00:37:54.806 --> 00:37:56.001
(DISTORTED VOICE) <i>You lied.</i>

654
00:37:56.074 --> 00:37:57.074
(ECHOES)

655
00:37:57.308 --> 00:37:58.308
What?

656
00:37:58.376 --> 00:38:01.039
<i>You stole the cages.
You ratted the car.</i>

657
00:38:01.346 --> 00:38:02.473
<i>You killed him.</i>

658
00:38:02.580 --> 00:38:03.741
Whoa.

659
00:38:04.115 --> 00:38:05.344
How does he know that?

660
00:38:05.850 --> 00:38:07.045
You did it.

661
00:38:07.152 --> 00:38:08.362
He told me. and I
didn't believe him.

662
00:38:08.386 --> 00:38:10.548
<i>Now it's your turn.</i> SARAH: What?

663
00:38:13.925 --> 00:38:15.086
Oh. my God. It's Roddy.

664
00:38:15.193 --> 00:38:16.786
DJ Retchid Kat is Roddy.

665
00:38:16.928 --> 00:38:18.123
This isn't funny. man.

666
00:38:18.930 --> 00:38:20.626
Oh. my God. Oh. my God.

667
00:38:21.232 --> 00:38:22.359
Rats!

668
00:38:22.433 --> 00:38:24.095
RODDY: <i>You framed my dad.</i>

669
00:38:25.503 --> 00:38:27.495
MARVIN: They're everywhere!

670
00:38:31.242 --> 00:38:32.608
(ALL SCREAMING)

671
00:38:34.612 --> 00:38:36.547
HANK: Oh. God. This is not good.

672
00:38:37.015 --> 00:38:38.039
(SARAH SCREAMS)

673
00:38:41.886 --> 00:38:43.218
<i>How does it feel?</i>

674
00:38:45.089 --> 00:38:47.558
(SHRIEKS) Oh. my
God! Oh. my God!

675
00:38:48.626 --> 00:38:50.026
Dude. let's go! Go! Go!

676
00:38:50.495 --> 00:38:51.929
Run! SARAH: Please
get them off me!

677
00:38:51.996 --> 00:38:53.294
Get them off! Get them off!

678
00:38:53.865 --> 00:38:54.924
RODDY: Sarah!

679
00:38:54.999 --> 00:38:56.092
Get off! Get off!

680
00:38:56.367 --> 00:38:57.562
(GUN FIRING)

681
00:38:58.636 --> 00:38:59.865
NICK: Oh. my God.

682
00:39:01.206 --> 00:39:02.834
Hang on!

683
00:39:09.447 --> 00:39:10.847
(WHIMPERING)

684
00:39:13.384 --> 00:39:15.319
TREY: We didn't mean
it. It was an accident.

685
00:39:15.486 --> 00:39:16.920
We never meant
to hurt Dr. Lawson.

686
00:39:17.755 --> 00:39:18.984
We just wanted to scare him.

687
00:39:19.123 --> 00:39:20.557
And make it look
like Roddy did it

688
00:39:20.625 --> 00:39:21.991
so Carter could take his place.

689
00:39:24.229 --> 00:39:25.720
Roddy was better than all of us.

690
00:39:28.166 --> 00:39:29.964
Will you tell him
that I'm sorry?

691
00:39:30.468 --> 00:39:31.731
Maybe you should do that.

692
00:39:35.440 --> 00:39:37.875
Guess they're going to
have to face the music.

693
00:39:38.042 --> 00:39:39.442
Really? You went there?

694
00:39:40.645 --> 00:39:42.238
Somebody had to.

695
00:39:53.124 --> 00:39:54.319
You want my weapon?

696
00:39:57.161 --> 00:39:59.255
Sarah had nothing to do with it.

697
00:39:59.497 --> 00:40:01.159
And she didn't
know her friends did.

698
00:40:04.736 --> 00:40:05.965
Was this worth it?

699
00:40:06.471 --> 00:40:07.471
They deserved it.

700
00:40:07.705 --> 00:40:08.905
Yeah. that's not what I asked.

701
00:40:09.507 --> 00:40:11.135
They never would've
admitted anything.

702
00:40:14.312 --> 00:40:16.645
Can't say I ever used
rats to get a confession.

703
00:40:19.250 --> 00:40:20.513
You're lucky no one got hurt.

704
00:40:22.987 --> 00:40:24.580
Except Dr. Lawson.

705
00:40:28.126 --> 00:40:29.253
Mmm!

706
00:40:29.427 --> 00:40:31.259
How many rats? What?

707
00:40:31.596 --> 00:40:34.259
For the report. How many rats
do you think were down there?

708
00:40:34.532 --> 00:40:35.852
I'm sorry. I didn't
stop to count.

709
00:40:35.934 --> 00:40:37.878
I'd like to put a million. 'cause
that's what it seemed like.

710
00:40:37.902 --> 00:40:39.813
Put a thousand. No one's
going to believe a million.

711
00:40:39.837 --> 00:40:41.430
Nobody's going to
believe a thousand.

712
00:40:42.507 --> 00:40:43.984
What are we going
to charge this kid with?

713
00:40:44.008 --> 00:40:46.705
Well. if it was up
to me... Nothing.

714
00:40:46.778 --> 00:40:48.055
We got to charge
him with something.

715
00:40:48.079 --> 00:40:49.723
He took a bunch of
kids and tried to hurt 'em.

716
00:40:49.747 --> 00:40:52.581
With music and rats and violins?

717
00:40:54.385 --> 00:40:56.251
No one forced those
kids to go down there.

718
00:40:56.454 --> 00:40:59.049
So all we got on Roddy is an
illegal rave with five people?

719
00:40:59.123 --> 00:41:02.243
D.A.'s not going to want this. plus
they got to deal with all those other kids.

720
00:41:04.395 --> 00:41:05.886
How's a kid do
something like that?

721
00:41:06.364 --> 00:41:08.629
Well. he was an outsider.

722
00:41:09.968 --> 00:41:10.968
He got pushed too far.

723
00:41:11.169 --> 00:41:13.649
No. no. I got that. I'm talking
about how he got all those rats

724
00:41:13.705 --> 00:41:15.003
to go down to that building.

725
00:41:16.507 --> 00:41:18.942
Oh. I don't know.

726
00:41:19.043 --> 00:41:20.187
There are a lot
of rats in the city.

727
00:41:20.211 --> 00:41:21.304
Maybe they like raves.

728
00:41:21.379 --> 00:41:22.745
Hmm. It was a rat rave.

729
00:41:23.247 --> 00:41:24.447
Do not put that in the report.

730
00:41:24.582 --> 00:41:25.582
(CHUCKLES)

731
00:41:26.651 --> 00:41:28.119
Want a slice? Sure.

732
00:41:29.120 --> 00:41:30.418
Oh! (LAUGHS)

733
00:41:31.489 --> 00:41:32.787
Damn! That's not funny!

734
00:41:32.857 --> 00:41:34.849
My man. Oh. it's funny
if you knew it was there.

735
00:41:34.993 --> 00:41:37.622
Chuckle now. but payback's
a bitch and she bites.

736
00:41:37.762 --> 00:41:38.762
(SQUEAKS)

737
00:41:40.298 --> 00:41:41.322
This will remind me.

738
00:41:50.108 --> 00:41:51.804
(KNOCKING AT DOOR)

739
00:41:56.547 --> 00:41:57.742
Uh. I waited until he left.

740
00:41:57.882 --> 00:41:59.960
I just want to get my tools.
and I'll be out of your hair.

741
00:41:59.984 --> 00:42:02.385
(NERVOUSLY) I don't want
any trouble. I'm a peaceful man.

742
00:42:02.553 --> 00:42:04.886
It's all right. He doesn't
even remember you.

743
00:42:05.223 --> 00:42:07.624
Uh. what do you mean? From
whatever time he arrested you.

744
00:42:07.692 --> 00:42:09.558
Arrested? What are
you talking about?

745
00:42:10.261 --> 00:42:11.701
Isn't that what
you're talking about?

746
00:42:11.863 --> 00:42:14.103
Look. you're never going to
see me again. I swear to God.

747
00:42:15.600 --> 00:42:17.034
What about the refrigerator?

748
00:42:17.402 --> 00:42:18.734
They're sending
another guy over.

749
00:42:18.970 --> 00:42:20.063
Why can't you just fix it?

750
00:42:20.138 --> 00:42:21.162
Look. lady.

751
00:42:21.539 --> 00:42:23.484
I don't know what kind of
games you two are playing here.

752
00:42:23.508 --> 00:42:25.670
I got three kids at
home. I don't need this.

753
00:42:25.777 --> 00:42:26.836
I never did anything bad.

754
00:42:26.911 --> 00:42:28.345
He's got no reason
to come after me.

755
00:42:28.513 --> 00:42:30.778
Please make sure he knows that.

755
00:42:31.305 --> 00:43:31.397
